   264	    """
   265	    Read marked blue arrow sprites as diagonal endpoints, connect same-marked arrow pairs, then emit rays from magenta cells on those diagonals.
   266	
   267	    Input structure:
   268	    - bg = most common color. Blue source objects are 3-cell L-shaped arrows whose corner cell is the tip and whose missing quadrant gives the forward diagonal.
   269	    - Each arrow has one orthogonally adjacent marker cell in a non-blue, non-magenta color. Marker colors that appear twice define the active arrow pairs.
   270	    - Magenta trigger cells may lie on the interior of active diagonals; uniquely marked arrows or off-diagonal magenta cells can appear as distractors.
   271	
   272	    Rule:
   273	    - Parse every valid blue arrow, group arrows by marker color, and for each marker color that labels exactly two arrows, draw the blue diagonal segment between their tips.
   274	    - While tracing that segment, only magenta cells act as triggers: from each such cell, launch magenta rays in both directions along the perpendicular diagonal, filling background cells until the boundary.
   275	
