    20	#    - Each arrow also has exactly one orthogonally adjacent marker cell in a non-blue,
    21	#      non-magenta color. Marker colors are the pairing labels: two arrows with the same marker
    22	#      color form one active pair. The segment is drawn between their tips, and both arrows must
    23	#      face toward that segment.
    24	#    - Example: suppose arrows A and B have red markers. A's tip is at (3,3) and points SE;
    25	#      B's tip is at (8,8) and points NW. Old logic would incorrectly read many blue cell pairs
    26	#      inside the arrow bodies and could not tell which blue cells are endpoints. New logic first
    27	#      parses each 4-connected 3-cell L, extracts its tip/direction, groups arrows by marker
